KG42.register("rules-289bb365a990e7a42ddae75d",{"id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R010","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R010","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Prosumer participation","process_stage":"participation","market_meaning":"Participating prosumers must take responsibility for maintaining their own power balance. Scope: Participation in the studied LEM; the responsibility is stated for the paper's broader prosumer category, including producers and consumers.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function participation.prosumer under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["participation.prosumer"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"participation","context_text":"Participation in the studied LEM; the responsibility is stated for the paper's broader prosumer category, including producers and consumers.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e04","v141-b-g03-E10"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Participating prosumers must take responsibility for maintaining their own power balance. Scope: Participation in the studied LEM; the responsibility is stated for the paper's broader prosumer category, including producers and consumers.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["participation.prosumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e04","v141-b-g03-E10"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e04","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"s, participants in the modeled LEM. Retailers and prosumers are currently rs implemented as agents i","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The core of lemlab is formed by the agents, which are active participants in the modeled LEM. Retailers and prosumers are currently implemented as agents in lemlab. Retailers are intermediaries that link the LEM to the wholesale market. They can purchase excess energy in the market or import energy from outside to meet energy demand. They typically offer fixed buy and sell prices and serves as the link to the wholesale market. In contrast, prosumers are physical agents operating household appliances that generate, consume, or store energy. Prosumers are capable of optimizing the operational plans of household appliances based on predictions. For the sake of simplification, we will use the term ''prosumers'' to refer to both producers and consumers in this study."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E10","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p13-c2r2__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":13,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"ameters on the average daily cost. m- The results suggest that HPs play a key role in achieving cost","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-13.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"LEMs require prosumers to take responsibility for maintaining their own power balance, which can incur balancing costs in cases where there are disparities between their predicted electrical loads and the actual consumption, as well as between PV production and feed-in power. This differs from with conventional electricity sales, where prices are fixed and settled after consumption. Therefore, these balancing costs can potentially undermine the economic advantages of LEMs."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"This rule defines a participation responsibility, not a design selection or operational decision variable. The cited source text does not define an x-type decision variable for this rule.","empty_theta_reason":"This rule defines a participation responsibility, not a fixed numeric or symbolic parameter. The cited source text does not define any theta-type parameter for this rule."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-participation","v141-a-M01-settlement"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"participation.prosumer","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E10","quote":"LEMs require prosumers to take responsibility for maintaining their own power balance"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e04","quote":"For the sake of simplification, we will use the term ''prosumers'' to refer to both producers and consumers in this study."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"a5d7301f186a97ba3a71cce38579fcc065a9418990a9d31728ba321702660e23","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The frozen rule states a qualitative participation obligation: prosumers participating in the LEM are required to take responsibility for maintaining their own power balance. Evidence v141-b-g03-E10 states this responsibility and notes possible balancing costs when predicted load or PV production differs from actual delivery; evidence v141-b-g01-e04 defines prosumers as the study's broader category for producers and consumers. Neither evidence defines an equation, decision variable, parameter, numeric bound, or optimization role for this participation responsibility. Therefore no supported mathematical expression is present, and the rule is recorded as a non-mathematical procedural constraint rather than inventing one.","bindings":[],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
